<title>GREECE: Greek/Bund gap widens to 355 bps, 246 vs BTP.</title>
<headline>Greek/Bund gap widens to 355 bps, 246 vs BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The spread of Greece's 10-year bond over bunds widened to 355 basis points today from 345 on Tuesday on the heels of higher drachma funding cost and gains in bunds at 1033 GMT.</p>
<p>The Greek/BTP gap also widened to 248 basis points from 232 yesterday on the back of strong gains by the Italian bond linked to EMU-related optimism.</p>
<p>		 CPN     MATURITY    YIELDS    SPREADS</p>
<p>   GREECE    8.80%   25JUN07	9.19%</p>
<p>   GERMANY   6.0%    04JUL07	5.64%    355 bps</p>
<p>   FRANCE    5.5%    25APR07	5.52%    367 bps</p>
<p>   ITALY     6.75%   01FEB07	6.73%    246 bps</p>
<p>   PORTUGAL  6.63%   23FEB07	6.37%    282 bps</p>
<p>   SPAIN     7.35%   31MAR07	6.35%    284 bps</p>
<p>   UK	  7.25%   07DEC07	7.10%    209 bps</p>
<p>   US	  6.63%   15MAY07	6.54%    265 bps</p>
<p>All yields are annualised and based on bid prices.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
